            <ArticleTitle>Giant adrenal pseudocyst.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>741-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">0131612/AIM.0012</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Adrenal cysts are rare lesions which are usually nonfunctional and asymptomatic. Adrenal pseudocysts do not have epithelial linings and account for about 40% of adrenal cysts. We report a case of giant adrenal pseudocyst in a 32 year old woman presenting with flank pain who had undergone surgical excision.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
